# Which environment this is. The only thing this file decides.
#
# The settings themselves live in `.env.<environment>`, so switching target is
# the one word below rather than swapping blocks of credentials in and out:
#
#   local        -> .env.local          committed; works with docker compose
#   development  -> .env.development    yours to create, never committed
#   production   -> .env.production     yours to create, never committed
#
# `docker compose up` ignores this and always runs the local stack, because the
# MongoDB and Redis it starts are the ones it points at. The switch matters when
# the service is run directly against a real datastore:
#
#   uv run -m app.main
#
ENVIRONMENT=local
